45 · SURVEY PARTICIPANTS

Mixed-methods study spanning majors, academic years, and residency statuses to capture a broad behavioral picture.

Financial behavior, social behavior, gamification, and emotional motivation — synthesized into one product concept.

Gen Z students understand that financial planning matters, but consistently disengage from budgeting tools that feel corporate, intimidating, and restrictive. Traditional apps overwhelm users with charts and treat spending as a problem — not a lifestyle.

Reframe budgeting as a socially connected lifestyle system — emotionally intelligent, passively tracked, and gamified — so financial awareness becomes motivating rather than anxiety-inducing.

Semi-structured interviews explored how students currently manage money, why budgeting tools fail to retain engagement, and what motivates long-term app usage.

The platform automatically tracks spending and transforms transactions into personalized insights — without punishing users for spending money.

Small wins and achievable goals — visible community progress and social accountability tied to friends and shared financial targets.

Users override AI category labels — corrections are stored in a personal database and improve future categorization automatically over time.

WayFinding

https://dhruvi0805.github.io/final_portfolio/pages/work-wayfinding.html

Students often struggle to navigate the library, leading to frustration, wasted time, and underutilization of resources. The library lacks an accessible wayfinding system integrated with its existing database.

Create a solution that improves physical navigation in the library while increasing efficiency and accessibility for all users.

Field research was conducted directly in the library environment — observing real navigation patterns, interviewing students mid-session, and mapping the most common points of confusion and abandonment.

Book search and guided routing from any point in the library — scan a QR code to transfer your route to your phone instantly.

Bluetooth beacon network provides turn-by-turn routing inside the library — no GPS signal required.

Proximity-based haptic feedback provides non-visual navigation cues for users with visual impairments — designed for one-handed use.

Routing engine and beacon management layer connects to the library's existing catalog database — no manual location tagging required.

70% · FASTER NAVIGATION

Average navigation time reduced to ~9.5 minutes across all user testing sessions.

64% · EASE OF USE

Self-reported ease-of-use improvement across all testing sessions with real library users.

ResearchGate

